{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793805293,"nonce":"24pifGtcCv0ON/mwo7J5+o25CQc=","message":"Final implementation: same-typed scalar store-to-load forwarding in the late single-entry-region cleanup, followed by bounded block-local overwritten-store removal. Provenance only adds fresh allocation versus global disjointness; unknown aliases, partial/reinterpreted/pointer-carrier stores, calls, volatile/atomic accesses and cold exits remain conservative. Global dead-store keys use storage identity, not SSA identity. The cleanup uses inline SmallVec storage and runs only after an actual forwarding hit.\n\nPlacement matters: early forwarding perturbed inlining and caused a repeatable Cranelift-only binary_trees slowdown. The final version runs after inlining. Its 21-pair binary_trees Cranelift-only medians are 144.164 -\u003e 144.069 ms wall, 126.827 -\u003e 125.950 ms timed region. The lambda_call startup control is 10.435 -\u003e 10.518 ms wall (21 pairs); no startup win claimed.\n\nNUC frozen-binary alternating comparisons against de05abe979c2142cdb4271d3ece10907919c23d8, taskset 0,2,4,6, exclusive lock, cooldown and per-sample thermal/load gates, no cargo/rustc between runs:\n- LLVM enabled, method_call 100,000 iterations, 21 pairs: wall 30.148 -\u003e 30.285 ms; timed region 3.637 -\u003e 2.806 ms (22.8% lower).\n- LLVM enabled, 1,000,000 iterations, 11 pairs: wall 57.753 -\u003e 49.665 ms (14.0% lower); timed region 29.010 -\u003e 20.706 ms (28.6% lower).\n- LLVM disabled by unsetting ZYLUA_LLVM and verifying backend=cranelift, short 21 pairs: wall 29.967 -\u003e 29.297 ms; timed region 3.450 -\u003e 2.684 ms (22.2% lower).\n- LLVM disabled, long 11 pairs: wall 53.468 -\u003e 46.164 ms (13.7% lower); timed region 26.727 -\u003e 19.792 ms (25.9% lower).\nThe benchmark os.clock region includes any work performed during that region; it is not an isolated machine-code throughput measure. Short wall remains startup dominated. Prior LuaJIT long reference remains about 17.3 ms wall / 15.4 ms timed, so the broader method_call gap stays open.\n\nValidation of final source: 28 focused compiler tests including actual interpreter/Cranelift/LLVM execution, Clippy -D warnings, 56 Lua release tests (including official, official_complete and warm-up checks against unchanged known failures), 50 Python release conformance tests, and all 1,413 local TS profile checks. Complete pinned TypeScript corpus: 5,948/5,948 files; PASS 1,151 / FAIL 12 / UNSUPPORTED 2,234 / SKIP 3,428, with zero per-case regressions and unchanged coverage/baseline. Existing unsupported/skipped/known failures are not compatibility passes.\n\nFinal NUC sweep: all 17 Lua kernels plus the extended method_call run match Lua 5.4, and all 22 supported Python kernels match CPython checksums. pidigits remains explicitly unsupported. No throttle-counter changes across 364 final timed samples. The three-sample Lua sweep and one-sample Python sweep are smoke checks, not claims of precise speed changes in unrelated kernels.\n\nFinal NUC Cranelift HIR/VCODE confirms the change: whole-chunk loads 142 -\u003e 103 and stores 262 -\u003e 215. The first Toggle loop now has one boolean XOR and two field stores instead of ten load/XOR/store sequences; the first store is retained before the pending-error exit, preserving observable state. Source-position stores needed at that exit remain. The remaining invariant pending-error branch and line bookkeeping are separate opportunities, not removed by weakening semantics.\n\nEvidence: /private/tmp/zyntax-store-forward/nuc-evidence.tar.gz, SHA256 959d9dd9d6ea8a84e8da458a7f37388228c13ae03e362fb9ec01c2f9d07981da. Includes raw timings, thermal records, scripts, binary hashes and final HIR/VCODE. Local validation reports and source hashes are alongside it in v4-* files. Post-run binary hashes match pre-run hashes. The dump metadata script initially included a directory in its binary-name filter; its filter was corrected and hashes verified without rerunning timings. No baseline or expected-output files changed.","files":null}]}